cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use linus, please cite it as below, together with the methods, functionals, basis sets and libxc you use."
type: software
title: "linus: Hartree-Fock and Kohn-Sham DFT energies, analytic gradients and Hessians"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch Hartree-Fock and Kohn-Sham DFT program with a Rust core and a Python
  front end that speaks qcdata: energies, analytic gradients and analytic Hessians,
  frequencies and thermochemistry, for closed and open shells, with global,
  range-separated and VV10 functionals, D3(BJ)/D4 dispersion, effective core potentials
  and implicit solvent (PCM, SMD), on CPUs and NVIDIA GPUs.
authors:
  - given-names: Colton
    family-names: Hicks
    affiliation: "Atoms for Humanity (Astera)"
version: 0.1.2
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/atomsforhumanity/linus"
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - density functional theory
  - Hartree-Fock
  - analytic Hessians
